{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the cloud departed from over the Tent.</b> This cloud — had it been the cloud that descended for the honor of Moses, which was mentioned above, ״ויעמוד פתח האהל״ — it would have been fitting to say, והענן סר מפתח האהל. Therefore it is possible to explain that it is the cloud by which Israel journeyed and encamped all the days of the wilderness, and since it departed from over the Tent, Israel supposed they would travel after it as was their custom, but the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded them to delay seven days — this is what is said: ״תסגר שבעת ימים.״ And when it says ״והעם לא נסע,״ it is as if it said that the cloud did not ascend, for it had departed from over the Tent for a sign, but it did not ascend until the seven days were completed; and the matter was so that it would be known and publicized to all Israel that their delay there seven days was for the honor of Miriam."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:51.789556830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}